    "narrative": "For May 7, 2026, the LawDog offense is anchored by two high-upside plays: **Tyler Freeman** (72.53) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (72.39). **Tyler Freeman** finds himself in an ideal scenario batting third against Scott, where a significant park boost (+14%) and favorable SP skill metrics elevate his efficiency well above his baseline. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** continues to be our most reliable engine; despite a slight discount for the matchup against Lugo, his high floor and favorable spot in the order keep him firmly in \"Strong\" territory. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** (63.53) remains a priority start; while his raw projections are modest, the \"slow delivery\" factor of Ginn provides a crucial opening for him to exploit the stolen base category, which remains our primary objective in 5x5 Roto.\n\nWe are navigating a few tricky matchups that necessitate careful bench management. **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.16) remains a locked-in starter due to his leadoff role (+10% bump), which is vital for our Runs category, though he faces a respectable arm in Keller. On the periphery, **Jeremiah Jackson** (42.74) represents our most marginal start; his inclusion is largely a volume play, as his score sits perilously close to the \"Below floor\" threshold due to his low spot in the order (-8%). While the bench is thinned out by team off-days for **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, and **Matt Chapman**, plus the unfortunate IL status of **Yainer Diaz**, our available depth\u2014including **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Wenceel Perez**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert**\u2014will be monitored closely for late-breaking lineup changes to ensure we aren't leaving potential points on the table.\n\nRisk management is centered on the **Taylor Ward** (46.27) and **Masyn Winn** (50.23) slots. **Taylor Ward** is dealing with a dual disadvantage of a subpar park and an unfavorable platoon matchup, which suppressed his score despite a premium spot in the batting order. We are proceeding with caution here; if official lineups confirm significant defensive shifts or further degradation in the matchup profile, we will be ready to pivot. As it stands, the combination of **Jonathan Aranda**'s mid-range utility and the high-speed potential of **Lawrence Butler** against Painter gives us a balanced roster that maximizes our exposure to steals without sacrificing our total base production.",
